    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p>Last updated: June 8, 2026</p>
    <p>I run HighSpeedRail.TV as a personal project: a curated collection of videos about high-speed rail. This page explains what happens to your information when you visit.</p>
    <p>The short version: I collect as little as possible, I don't sell anything about you, and the only thing I ever ask for directly is your email, if you decide to subscribe.</p>
    <h2>What I collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Newsletter signups. If you enter your email to subscribe, I store it so I can send you the newsletter. That's the only reason I have it. You can unsubscribe from any issue and your address comes off the list.</li>
      <li>Analytics. I use Google Analytics to see roughly how many people visit and which videos get watched, which tells me what to curate more of. It's aggregate traffic data, not a profile of you by name.</li>
      <li>Server logs. Like any website, my host (Cloudflare) keeps standard access logs for security and performance.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Embedded videos</h2>
    <p>The videos here are embedded from YouTube in its privacy-enhanced mode (youtube-nocookie.com), which holds off on setting tracking cookies until you actually press play. Once you play a video, YouTube's own privacy policy takes over.</p>
    <h2>What I don't do</h2>
    <p>I don't sell, rent, or trade your information, and I don't run ad networks. There's no login and no account, so there's nothing of yours sitting here to break into beyond a newsletter email.</p>
    <h2>If you're in the EU or UK</h2>
    <p>You can ask what I hold about you, correct it, or have it deleted. For this site that's almost always just your newsletter email, so email me and I'll take care of it. I don't use a cookie-consent banner because the site doesn't set advertising cookies.</p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about your data: hello@highspeedrail.tv</p>
  </div>
</section>
